                      (   unit_tests.asm):00285         ; TSTSYSIO - System/Console I/O tests (glossary section 3.1, 12
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00286         ; words, 7 tests). Six words are deliberately NOT tested here -
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00287         ; KEY, ACCEPT, EXPECT, and QUERY all genuinely block on real
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00288         ; input during automated, headless boot-time testing (confirmed
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00289         ; by reading their own implementations: KEY spins on itself,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00290         ; ACCEPT calls KEY directly, EXPECT/QUERY both call ACCEPT); and
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00291         ; ABORT/QUIT are both designed to never return (ABORT falls
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00292         ; through into QUIT, which resets the return stack, discarding
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00293         ; this entire call chain and hijacking the boot sequence into
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00294         ; the interpreter's own top-level loop). See this group's own
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00295         ; leading comment block, right before TSTKEYQ, for the full
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00296         ; reasoning.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00297         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00298         ; EMIT/TYPE/CR/SPACE/SPACES are safe and already proven so - this
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00299         ; whole test framework has used TYPE and CR (via TSTREPORT)
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00300         ; thousands of times already across every prior test group.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00301         ; Each test here verifies the real queuing mechanism (OUTHEAD/
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00302         ; OUTBUF), reading the actual character(s) back out of the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00303         ; output ring buffer to confirm they were genuinely queued, not
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00304         ; just that the call returned without crashing.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):00305         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
