                      (   unit_tests.asm):03332         ; TSTDARITH - mixed & double-precision arithmetic tests (glossary
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03333         ; section 3.5). Covers every word in that section. All 14 words
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03334         ; traced by hand against their real implementations before any
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03335         ; test was written - push/pop order for double-cell values (low
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03336         ; cell pushed first, high cell last/on top - confirmed identical
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03337         ; across every word here), and which of two operands is which
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03338         ; (d1 vs d2, dividend vs divisor) - not assumed from the glossary
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03339         ; stack-effect notation alone. FM/MOD (floored) and SM/REM
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03340         ; (symmetric) tested against the same negative-dividend case
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03341         ; specifically because that's where the two conventions actually
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03342         ; diverge - confirmed distinct expected results for each.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):03343         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
