                      (   unit_tests.asm):07157         ; TSTDEFWORDS - defining-words tests (glossary section 3.9, 17
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07158         ; words, 12 tests since VALUE/TO and IS/ACTION-OF are each
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07159         ; combined into one test). Every defining word parses a name
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07160         ; from the input source via WORD (HEADER's own mechanism,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07161         ; shared by :/CREATE) - a complexity nothing in section 3.8 had.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07162         ; Each test redirects CODEHERE, DPHERE, VARHERE, and
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07163         ; SRCADDR/SRCLEN/TOIN together (a fake name, "TESTWD", reused
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07164         ; safely across every test here since each redirect/restore
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07165         ; cycle is fully isolated), calls the real defining word
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07166         ; directly, saves the newly-defined word's own CFA (= CODEHERE
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07167         ; at the moment the defining word was called), restores
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07168         ; everything, then executes that CFA directly to verify runtime
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07169         ; behavior.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07170         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07171         ; A real, structurally important finding from this section:
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07172         ; HEADER writes to the real LATEST variable unconditionally, not
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07173         ; a redirectable copy like CODEHERE/DPHERE/VARHERE - every test
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07174         ; here explicitly saves and restores it, confirmed necessary by
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07175         ; reading HEADER's own code directly, not assumed safe by analogy
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07176         ; with the other three pointers.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07177         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07178         ; MARKER's own test is the one exception to the general
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07179         ; redirect-then-restore-then-execute order: DOMARKER (confirmed
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07180         ; by reading it directly) writes to the real DPHERE/CODEHERE/
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07181         ; VARHERE/LATEST unconditionally too, so that test executes the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07182         ; marker word while still redirected, only restoring the real
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07183         ; environment afterward - getting this order backwards would
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07184         ; have corrupted the real dictionary pointers with scratch
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07185         ; addresses.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07186         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07187         ; Bare CREATE (never followed by DOES>) is deliberately not
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07188         ; tested on its own - traced its placeholder "behavior field"
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07189         ; (a genuine compiled JSR DOESRT0 instruction) and confirmed
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07190         ; DODOES reads that field as raw data, not as code to execute -
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07191         ; which only produces a valid jump target for the raw-address
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07192         ; form every other defining word uses (VARIABLE, CONSTANT, etc,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07193         ; via CODECOMMA), not CREATE's own placeholder JSR instruction.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07194         ; Bare CREATE's own direct-execution behavior isn't meant to be
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07195         ; relied upon before a DOES> patches it.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):07196         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
