                      (   unit_tests.asm):08715         ; traced MARKERW's own code and confirmed its internal snapshot
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08716         ; is taken at its very start, before HEADER or any compiling
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08717         ; runs at all, so that's genuinely the correct restore target,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08718         ; not assumed.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08719         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08720         ; DOMARKER (confirmed by reading it directly) writes to the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08721         ; real DPHERE/CODEHERE/VARHERE/LATEST unconditionally, not to
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08722         ; any redirected copy - so this test must execute the marker
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08723         ; word while CODEHERE/DPHERE/VARHERE are still redirected (their
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08724         ; real values are restored only afterward), unlike every other
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08725         ; test in this section, which restores first and executes
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08726         ; second. Getting this order backwards would have corrupted the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08727         ; real dictionary pointers with scratch addresses.
