                      (   unit_tests.asm):08882         ; TSTCOMPWORDS - compiling-words tests (glossary section 3.10,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08883         ; 13 words, 17 tests since several get separate cases: TICK
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08884         ; found/not-found, ['] compiling/interpreting state, POSTPONE
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08885         ; normal/immediate word, SLITERAL compiling/interpreting state,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08886         ; ABORT" false/true flag). Reuses the scratch infrastructure
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08887         ; established for sections 3.8/3.9 throughout.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08888         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08889         ; POSTPONE is this section's hardest case: a genuine two-level
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08890         ; compile-time mechanism. Traced its own code first - for a
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08891         ; normal word, it compiles code that ITSELF compiles a call to
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08892         ; that word later, when the current definition eventually runs,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08893         ; not immediately (standard ANS semantics: POSTPONE appends a
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08894         ; word's own compilation semantics to the current definition,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08895         ; and for an ordinary word that semantics IS "compile a call to
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08896         ; it", so appending it only makes sense if the current
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08897         ; definition later performs that compiling action itself,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08898         ; against whatever's being compiled at that later point).
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08899         ; Verified via the compiled byte sequence directly rather than
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08900         ; fully executing a triple-nested compile chain.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08901         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08902         ; ABORT" is safely testable for both its flag cases - confirmed
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08903         ; by reading its own runtime code that it uses THROW -2
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08904         ; internally, not the raw, never-returns ABORT mechanism plain
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08905         ; ABORT itself uses (still deliberately untested, per section
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08906         ; 3.1's own reasoning).
                      (   unit_tests.asm):08907         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
