                      (   unit_tests.asm):09621         ; TSTPOSTPONE1 - unit test for POSTPONE, normal (non-immediate)
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09622         ; word case. Traced its own code first: for a normal word,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09623         ; POSTPONE compiles "[LIT xt][JSR COMPILE,]" into the current
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09624         ; definition - NOT a direct call to the word itself. This is
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09625         ; standard ANS semantics (POSTPONE appends a word's own
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09626         ; compilation semantics to the current definition; for an
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09627         ; ordinary word, that semantics IS "compile a call to it", so
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09628         ; the current definition, when it later runs, must itself
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09629         ; perform that compiling action against whatever definition is
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09630         ; being compiled at that later point - not immediately). Given
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09631         ; the genuine complexity of fully executing that second level
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09632         ; (which would need a further redirected CODEHERE and a further
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09633         ; round of execute-and-verify), this test instead verifies the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09634         ; compiled byte sequence directly - still a meaningful,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09635         ; unambiguous check of POSTPONE's own documented mechanism.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):09636         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
