                      (   unit_tests.asm):11434         ; TSTSTRPARSE - strings & parsing tests (glossary section 3.12,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11435         ; 16 words, 19 tests since several get separate cases: [CHAR]
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11436         ; compiling/interpreting state, S" compiling/interpreting state
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11437         ; (this word genuinely has both), SEARCH found/not-found,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11438         ; REPLACES/SUBSTITUTE combined across two tests (covering all 4
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11439         ; of SUBSTITUTE's own documented %-delimiter cases), SNAME
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11440         ; found/not-found.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11441         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11442         ; . has no STATE check at all in its own code (confirmed by
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11443         ; reading it directly - matches "no interpretation semantics,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11444         ; per ANS" without a specific -14 throw, unlike [CHAR]/S"), so
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11445         ; only its compiling case is tested. Its own runtime calls TYPE
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11446         ; internally, so its own test applies the SERIALPOLL-conditional
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11447         ; lesson from section 3.1 from the start, rather than
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11448         ; re-discovering it via a failed MAME run.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11449         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11450         ; SUBSTITUTE/REPLACES/UNESCAPE all carry extensive prior-session
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11451         ; bug-fix history in their own comments - confirmed fresh against
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11452         ; the actual current code (not re-derived from scratch), and
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11453         ; SUBSTITUTE's own expected outputs independently simulated in
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11454         ; Python against the traced algorithm before writing the tests,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11455         ; not hand-derived and assumed correct.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11456         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11457         ; Note: this section's own COMPARE (string comparison) word's
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11458         ; test is named TSTSCOMPARE, not TSTCOMPARE - the latter was
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11459         ; already taken by section 3.7's own comparison-operators group
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11460         ; wrapper, caught by the standard collision check before
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11461         ; insertion.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):11462         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
