                      (   unit_tests.asm):12186         ; throw, unlike [CHAR]/S"), so only the compiling case is
                      (   unit_tests.asm):12187         ; tested, matching how it's actually meant to be used. Its own
                      (   unit_tests.asm):12188         ; runtime (DOTSTR) calls TYPE internally, which has two entirely
                      (   unit_tests.asm):12189         ; different implementations gated by SERIALPOLL (the same real
                      (   unit_tests.asm):12190         ; finding from section 3.1) - applying that lesson from the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):12191         ; start here rather than re-discovering it: EMITCH works
                      (   unit_tests.asm):12192         ; universally for a single-character check, but this outputs
                      (   unit_tests.asm):12193         ; multiple characters, so - matching TSTCR's own established
                      (   unit_tests.asm):12194         ; fix - the full OUTHEAD/OUTBUF check only applies under
                      (   unit_tests.asm):12195         ; SERIALPOLL=0, with a narrower EMITCH-based check (last
                      (   unit_tests.asm):12196         ; character only, plus the stack-depth check) for SERIALPOLL=1.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):12197         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
