                      (   unit_tests.asm):13134         ; TSTNUMOUT - numeric output tests (glossary section 3.13, 14
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13135         ; words, 13 tests since #S and #> are combined into one test,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13136         ; matching how they're naturally used together as the tail of
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13137         ; the standard pictured-output idiom "<# ... #S #>").
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13138         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13139         ; The pictured-numeric-output core (<# # #S #> HOLD HOLDS) is
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13140         ; pure string-building with no I/O, tested directly. SIGN
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13141         ; carries real bug-fix history - a prior bare BPL right after
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13142         ; PULU didn't affect condition codes on real 6809 hardware, and
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13143         ; the bug was masked for every internal caller by caller-side
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13144         ; luck (each ran a flag-setting LDD right before calling SIGN).
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13145         ; This section's own SIGN test deliberately poisons the flags
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13146         ; with an unrelated CMPX immediately before each direct call,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13147         ; so it exercises the exact previously-broken scenario rather
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13148         ; than repeating the same kind of luck that hid the bug.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13149         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13150         ; The high-level printing words (./U./.R/U.R/?/D./D.R) all
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13151         ; produce real output via TYPE/EMIT internally, so each applies
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13152         ; the SERIALPOLL-conditional split established in section 3.1 -
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13153         ; full OUTHEAD/OUTBUF verification under SERIALPOLL=0, an
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13154         ; EMITCH-based last-character check under SERIALPOLL=1. .R/U.R/
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13155         ; D.R specifically test the padding path (a width wider than the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13156         ; actual digits), not just a no-padding sanity case. D./D.R use
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13157         ; a genuine double-cell value (-100000, computed and verified
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13158         ; independently in Python before writing the tests) to exercise
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13159         ; the 32-bit negation path, not a value that happens to fit in
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13160         ; one cell.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13161         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13162         ; Note: this section's own COMPARE-adjacent naming risk doesn't
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13163         ; apply here, but every group wrapper name (TSTNUMOUT) and every
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13164         ; internal FAIL/DONE prefix was still checked against the whole
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13165         ; file before insertion, per the standard practice that caught
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13166         ; the TSTCOMPARE collision in the prior section.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13167         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
