                      (   unit_tests.asm):13415         ; TSTSIGN - unit test for SIGN. Deliberately poisons the CPU
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13416         ; flags with an unrelated CMPX (setting them to reflect a
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13417         ; positive comparison result, without touching D or the value
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13418         ; about to be pushed) immediately before each PSHU/JSR SIGN
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13419         ; call - specifically so this test exercises the exact scenario
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13420         ; the word's own bug-fix comment says was previously broken (a
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13421         ; direct, standalone call not preceded by a flag-setting LDD of
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13422         ; the true value), rather than relying on the same kind of
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13423         ; caller-side luck that hid the original bug. Two sub-cases:
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13424         ; negative (with flags poisoned toward positive, confirming the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13425         ; minus sign still gets added - would fail if SIGN reverted to
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13426         ; testing stale flags instead of the value it just popped) and
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13427         ; positive (with flags poisoned toward negative, confirming no
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13428         ; minus sign gets added incorrectly).
                      (   unit_tests.asm):13429         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
