                      (   unit_tests.asm):15018         ; TSTENVSYS - environmental & system queries tests (glossary
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15019         ; section 3.17, 10 words, 8 tests since TIB/#TIB/>IN/SPAN/BL are
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15020         ; combined into one test, and ENVIRONMENT? gets three separate
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15021         ; tests of its own - single-cell, double-cell, and unsupported-
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15022         ; string cases).
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15023         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15024         ; REFILL genuinely blocks on real input when the source is the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15025         ; terminal (confirmed by reading its own code: the terminal
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15026         ; branch calls QUERY, which per section 3.1's own already-
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15027         ; established finding calls ACCEPT, which calls KEY, which spins
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15028         ; forever without real input) - only its safely-testable path
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15029         ; (source is a string) is tested here, matching the same
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15030         ; reasoning already applied to KEY/ACCEPT/EXPECT/QUERY
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15031         ; themselves. EVALUATE genuinely executes its given string as
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15032         ; real Forth source via JSR INTERPRET - confirmed safe via
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15033         ; INTERPRET's own code (it simply stops when input is exhausted,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15034         ; no automatic REFILL, so no blocking risk), making a short,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15035         ; deliberately harmless string ("1 2 +") safe to evaluate
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15036         ; directly.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15037         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15038         ; ENVIRONMENT? carries substantial, already-documented bug-fix
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15039         ; history (a COMPAREW-clobbers-X bug, confirmed via MAME with the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15040         ; exact $4E4D symptom). This section's own tests specifically
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15041         ; query "/COUNTED-STRING" immediately followed by "MAX-N" - the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15042         ; exact adjacent pair the bug-fix comment describes - so a
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15043         ; regression of that specific mechanism would be caught again,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15044         ; not just assumed fixed from the comment alone.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15045         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
