                      (   unit_tests.asm):15074         ; Environmental & System Queries test harness (glossary section
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15075         ; 3.17). Five words (TIB/#TIB/>IN/SPAN/BL) are simple constant/
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15076         ; variable readers, combined into one test rather than five
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15077         ; separate ones, matching the established approach from section
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15078         ; 3.14's own TSTBASE.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15079         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15080         ; REFILL genuinely blocks on real input when the source is the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15081         ; terminal (confirmed by reading its own code directly: the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15082         ; terminal branch calls QUERY, which - per section 3.1's own
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15083         ; already-established finding - calls ACCEPT, which calls KEY,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15084         ; which spins forever without real input). Only its safely-
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15085         ; testable path (source is a string, SRCID<>0) is tested here,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15086         ; matching the same reasoning already applied to KEY/ACCEPT/
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15087         ; EXPECT/QUERY themselves in section 3.1.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15088         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15089         ; EVALUATE genuinely executes its given string as real Forth
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15090         ; source via JSR INTERPRET - confirmed via INTERPRET's own code
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15091         ; that it simply stops and returns when input is exhausted (no
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15092         ; automatic REFILL, so no blocking risk), making a short,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15093         ; deliberately harmless string ("1 2 +") safe to evaluate
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15094         ; directly.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15095         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15096         ; ENVIRONMENT? carries substantial, already-documented bug-fix
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15097         ; history (a COMPAREW-clobbers-X bug, confirmed via MAME with the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15098         ; exact $4E4D symptom - reading two bytes of the NEXT table
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15099         ; entry's own name text as if they were the current entry's
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15100         ; value). This section's own tests specifically query
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15101         ; "/COUNTED-STRING" immediately followed by "MAX-N" - the exact
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15102         ; adjacent pair the bug-fix comment describes - so a regression
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15103         ; of that specific mechanism would be caught again, not just
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15104         ; assumed fixed from the comment alone.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15105         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15106         
