                      (   unit_tests.asm):15766         ; Tools test harness (glossary section 3.18). WORDS depends
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15767         ; directly on LATEST (confirmed via its own code: it walks from
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15768         ; LATEST until the chain terminates at 0) - the same real, pre-
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15769         ; COLD dependency section 3.17's own TSTEVALUATE was found to
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15770         ; need, so this section's own WORDS test redirects LATEST too,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15771         ; applying that lesson from the start rather than rediscovering
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15772         ; it. All three words produce visible output, so all apply the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15773         ; SERIALPOLL-conditional split established in section 3.1.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15774         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15775         ; .S prints the ENTIRE real data stack, including whatever this
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15776         ; whole calling chain (TSTRUNNER and everything above it) already
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15777         ; left there before this test even started - unlike every other
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15778         ; test in this session, there's no way to know the full, exact
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15779         ; output in advance. This test's own verification is deliberately
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15780         ; narrower as a result: confirms the core, documented guarantee
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15781         ; directly (the stack is genuinely unchanged afterward, non-
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15782         ; destructive for real) plus, in interrupt mode only (where the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15783         ; first characters queued are unambiguously this test's own top
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15784         ; value, since .S starts from the current top of stack), that the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15785         ; very first characters match - rather than attempting to predict
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15786         ; or verify the complete printed output.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15787         ;
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15788         ; DUMP carries real, already-documented bug-fix history: a prior
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15789         ; version's ASCII column read past the actual byte count on a
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15790         ; partial final line, showing garbage characters for the unused
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15791         ; portion - fixed via DUVALID tracking. This section's own test
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15792         ; specifically dumps a non-multiple-of-16 byte count (5), the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15793         ; exact scenario that bug affected, verifying the ASCII column's
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15794         ; own blanking for the remaining, invalid columns.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15795         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15796         
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15797         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15798         ; TSTDOTS - unit test for .S. Pushes two known values (no guard
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15799         ; sentinel below them, since .S would print that too), calls .S,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15800         ; and verifies the stack is genuinely unchanged afterward - the
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15801         ; core, documented "non-destructive" guarantee, confirmed
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15802         ; directly rather than inferred. In interrupt mode specifically,
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15803         ; also confirms the very first characters queued match the top
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15804         ; value's own printed form (unambiguous, since .S starts from
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15805         ; the current top of stack); polling mode only confirms some
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15806         ; output occurred, given EMITCH alone can't distinguish this
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15807         ; test's own output from whatever the rest of the real stack
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15808         ; contributes afterward.
                      (   unit_tests.asm):15809         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
