                      (    forth6809.asm):03776                                   ; (a real discard of the loop-control frame).
                      (    forth6809.asm):03777                                   ; EXIT's own EXITUNLOOP mechanism already
                      (    forth6809.asm):03778                                   ; discards the frame automatically and
                      (    forth6809.asm):03779                                   ; correctly on every path - traced and
                      (    forth6809.asm):03780                                   ; confirmed: with no enclosing DO (compiled
                      (    forth6809.asm):03781                                   ; count 0), with one enclosing DO and no
                      (    forth6809.asm):03782                                   ; prior UNLOOP (discards the full 8-byte
                      (    forth6809.asm):03783                                   ; frame correctly). The one combination that
                      (    forth6809.asm):03784                                   ; broke was UNLOOP immediately before EXIT -
                      (    forth6809.asm):03785                                   ; UNLOOP discarding 6 of the 8 bytes itself,
                      (    forth6809.asm):03786                                   ; then EXITUNLOOP unconditionally discarding
                      (    forth6809.asm):03787                                   ; a full 8 more, overshooting into whatever
                      (    forth6809.asm):03788                                   ; sat below (typically the caller's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):03789                                   ; return address) and branching into random
                      (    forth6809.asm):03790                                   ; memory on return. Since UNLOOP has no
                      (    forth6809.asm):03791                                   ; other legitimate use than immediately
                      (    forth6809.asm):03792                                   ; preceding an exit from the definition, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):03793                                   ; EXIT already handles that correctly on its
                      (    forth6809.asm):03794                                   ; own, UNLOOP is now a true no-op rather than
                      (    forth6809.asm):03795                                   ; a second, conflicting discard mechanism.
